d a purpose-built city. Official capital: Canberra \u00b7 Population of Canberra (2021): 484,630 \u00b7 Year named capital: 1913 \u00b7 Federal territory: Australian Capital [\u2026]", "timestamp": "2026-07-16T00:00:00", "url": "https://usanalysis.org/blog/what-is-the-capital-of-australia/", "meta_data": {"citation_domain_name": null, "client": "web", "images": []}, "is_attachment": false, "is_image": false, "is_code_interpreter": false, "is_knowledge_card": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_widget": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_client_context": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false}, "status": "UNSORTED", "citation": 4}, {"web_result": {"name": "Australia - Wikipedia", "snippet": "", "timestamp": "2001-11-04T00:00:00", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia", "meta_data": {"citation_domain_name": null, "client": "web", "images": ["https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Flag_of_Australia_%28converted%29.svg/1280px-Flag_of_Australia_%28converted%29.svg.png"]}, "is_attachment": false, "is_image": false, "is_code_interpreter": false, "is_knowledge_card": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_widget": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_client_context": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false, "trust": {"level": 2, "name": "trusted", "description": "is trusted for broad, cited secondary-reference information across education, science, history, and general knowledge"}}, "status": "UNSORTED", "citation": 5}, {"web_result": {"name": "Portal:Geography/Featured article/28 - Wikipedia", "snippet": "Canberra is the capital city of Australia and with a population of just over 323,000 is Australia's largest inland city. Canberra was selected as the location of the nation's capital in 1908 as a compromise between Sydney and Melbourne and is unusual amongst Australian capital cities as an entirely purpose-built, planned city.", "timestamp": "2022-01-01T00:00:00", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portal:Geography/Featured_article/28", "meta_data": {"citation_domain_name": null, "client": "web", "images": []}, "is_attachment": false, "is_image": false, "is_code_interpreter": false, "is_knowledge_card": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_widget": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_client_context": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false, "trust": {"level": 2, "name": "trusted", "description": "is trusted for broad, cited secondary-reference information across education, science, history, and general knowledge"}}, "status": "UNSORTED", "citation": 6}, {"web_result": {"name": "List of Australian capital cities - Wikipedia", "snippet": "There are eight capital cities in Australia, each of which functions as the seat of government for the state or territory in which it is located. One of these, Canberra, is also the national capital. Section 125 of the Constitution of Australia specified that the seat of the national government, that is, the national capital, would be in its own territory within New South Wales, at least 100 miles (161 km) from Sydney. The Constitution specified that until this national capital was ready, the...", "timestamp": "2005-12-05T00:00:00", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Australian_capital_cities", "meta_data": {"citation_domain_name": null, "client": "web", "images": ["https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Skylines_of_Sydney_CBD_seen_from_North_Sydney%2C_August_2022%2C_04.jpg/1280px-Skylines_of_Sydney_CBD_seen_from_North_Sydney%2C_August_2022%2C_04.jpg"]}, "is_attachment": false, "is_image": false, "is_code_interpreter": false, "is_knowledge_card": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_widget": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_client_context": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false, "trust": {"level": 2, "name": "trusted", "de