rom Melbourne in \\\", \\\"**192\\\", \\\"7**.[10][4][7][13]\\\", \\\"\\\\n\\\", \\\"## What makes Canberra uni\\\", \\\"que?\\\", \\\"\\\\n\\\", \\\"- It\\\\u2019s a **pur\\\", \\\"pose-built, planned \\\", \\\"city**, designed by Amer\\\", \\\"ican architect Wa\\\", \\\"lter Burley Grif\\\", \\\"fin.[6][13]\\\\n- \\\", \\\"It\\\\u2019s Austr\\\", \\\"alia\\\\u2019s **largest in\\\", \\\"land city**, located in\\\", \\\" the **Australian Capital Territo\\\", \\\"ry (ACT\\\", \\\")**, about\\\", \\\" 150\\\\u2013240 km south\\\", \\\"west of Syd\\\", \\\"ney.[3][10]\\\", \\\"[12]\\\\n- Unlike \\\", \\\"most nati\\\", \\\"onal capitals\\\", \\\", it was n\\\", \\\"ever a major commer\\\", \\\"cial or \\\", \\\"port \\\", \\\"city; it ex\\\", \\\"ists primarily as\\\", \\\" the **\\\", \\\"seat of govern\\\", \\\"men\\\", \\\"t**.\\\", \\\"[13][14]\\\", \\\"\\\\n\\\", \\\"So Sydney rem\\\", \\\"ains Australia\\\\u2019s largest\\\", \\\" and most internation\\\", \\\"ally recogn\\\", \\\"ized city, but Canb\\\", \\\"erra holds the official st\\\", \\\"atus of nati\\\", \\\"onal capita\\\", \\\"l as a deliberate compro\\\", \\\"mise to bal\\\", \\\"ance regional r\\\", \\\"ivalr\\\", \\\"ies.[2][11][15]\\\"], \\\"extra_web_results\\\": [], \\\"structured_answer\\\": [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"markdown\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"The capital of Australia is **Canberra**, not Sydney.[2][3][12]\\\", \\\"chunks\\\": [\\\"The capital of Australia is **Canberra**, not Sydney.[2][3][12]\\\"], \\\"images\\\": [], \\\"inline_token_annotations\\\": []}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"markdown\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"## Why Canberra, not Sydney?\\\", \\\"chunks\\\": [\\\"## Why Canberra, not Sydney?\\\"], \\\"images\\\": [], \\\"inline_token_annotations\\\": []}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"markdown\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"Canberra was chosen as Australia\\\\u2019s capital in **1908** as a political compromise between the country\\\\u2019s two largest and most rivalrous cities: **Sydney** and **Melbourne**.[4][6][10][11]\\\\n\\\\nWhen Australia federated in 1901, both Sydney (in New South Wales) and Melbourne (in Victoria) wanted to be the national capital. The dispute was so intense it threatened the unity of the new nation.[13][14]\\\\n\\\\nThe solution, written into **Section 125 of the Australian Constitution**, was:\\\\n\\\\n- The capital would be located **within New South Wales** (giving Sydney\\\\u2019s state the honor)  \\\\n- But it had to be **at least 100 miles (161 km) from Sydney** (so Sydney wouldn\\\\u2019t dominate)  \\\\n- Until the new capital was ready, **Melbourne would serve as the temporary seat of government**[7][15]\\\\n\\\\nCanberra, a rural area between the two cities, was selected in 1908, formally founded in **1913**, and the federal government finally moved there from Melbourne in **1927**.[10][4][7][13]\\\", \\\"chunks\\\": [\\\"Canberra was chosen as Australia\\\\u2019s capital in **1908** as a political compromise between the country\\\\u2019s two largest and most rivalrous cities: **Sydney** and **Melbourne**.[4][6][10][11]\\\\n\\\\nWhen Australia federated in 1901, both Sydney (in New South Wales) and Melbourne (in Victoria) wanted to be the national capital. The dispute was so intense it threatened the unity of the new nation.[13][14]\\\\n\\\\nThe solution, written into **Section 125 of the Australian Constitution**, was:\\\\n\\\\n- The capital would be located **within New South Wales** (giving Sydney\\\\u2019s state the honor)  \\\\n- But it had to be **at least 100 miles (161 km) from Sydney** (so Sydney wouldn\\\\u2019t dominate)  \\\\n- Until the new capital was ready, **Melbourne would serve as the temporary seat of government**[7][15]\\\\n\\\\nCanberra, a rural area between the two cities, was selected in 1908, formally founded in **1913**, and the federal government finally moved there from Melbourne in **1927**.[10][4][7][13]\\\"], \\\"images\\\": [], \\\"inline_token_annotations\\\": []}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"markdown\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"## What makes Canberra unique?\\\", \\\"chunks\\\": [\\\"## What makes Canberra unique?\\\"], \\\"images\\\": [], \\\"inline_token_annotations\\\": []}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"markdown\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"- It\\\\u2019s a **purpose-built, planned city**, designed by American architect Walter Burley Griffin.[6][13]\\\\n- It\\\\u2019s Australia\\\\u2019s **largest inland city**, located in the **Australian Capital Territory (ACT)**, about 150\\\\u2013240 km southwest of Sydney.[3][10][12]\\\\n- Unlike most national capitals, it was never a major commercial or port city; it exists primarily as the **seat of government**.[13][14]\\\", \\\"chunks\\\": [\\\"- It\\\\u2019s a **purpose-built, planned city**, designed by American architect Walter Burley Griffin.[6][13]\\\\n- It\\\\u2019s Australia\\\\u2019s **largest inland city**, located in the **Australian Capital Territory (ACT)**, about 150\\\\u2013240 km southwest of Sydney.[3][10][12]\\\\n- Unlike most national capitals, it was never a major commercial or port city; it exists primarily as the **seat of government**.[13][14]\\\"], \\\"images\\\": [{\\\"image_url\\\": \\\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/Overlooking_Canberra,_Parliament_House,_War_Memorial.jpg\\\", \\\"width\\\": 2517, \\\"height\\\": 1564, \\\"thumbnail\\\": \\\"https://d2u1z1lopyfwlx.cloudfront.net/thumbnails/27ddc6ff-34e4-5796-a9e8-305900caaab9/01a84265-e09c-5682-92ce-681c89a1afe2.jpg\\\", \\\"thumbnail_width\\\": 512, \\\"thumbnail_height\\\": 318, \\\"thumbnail_512\\\": null, \\\"thumbnail_512_smart\\\": null, \\\"source_url\\\": \\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Australian_capital_cities\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"List of Australian capital cities - Wikipedia\\\", \\\"caption\\\": \\\"View of Canberra showing the Australian War Memorial, Anzac Parade leading across Lake Burley Griffin towards Parliament House on Capital Hill.\\\", \\\"modal_url\\\": null, \\\"medium\\\": \\\"image\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"sapi_images\\\", \\\"generated_media_metadata\\\": null, \\\"original_image_url\\\": null}], \\\"inline_token_annotations\\\": []}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"markdown\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"So Sydney remains Australia\\\\u2019s largest and most internationally recognized city, but Canberra holds the official status of national capital as a deliberate compromise to balance regional rivalries.[2][11][15]\\\", \\\"chunks\\\": [\\\"So Sydney remains Australia\\\\u2019s largest and most internationally recognized city, but Canberra holds the official status of national capital as a deliberate compromise to balance regional rivalries.[2][11][15]\\\"], \\\"images\\\": [], \\\"inline_token_annotations\\\": []}]}\"}, \"uuid\": \"\"}]", "thread_title": "what is the capital of Australia and why is it not Sydney", "related_queries": ["Who was Walter Burley Griffin and how did he design Canberra", "What are the main government institutions located in Canberra", "How does Canberra compare to other planned capitals like Brasilia", "What is the significance of the Australian Capital Territory", "Are there other countries with capitals chosen as compromises"], "display_model": "pplx_pro", "user_selected_model": "pplx_pro", "personalized": true, "mode": "COPILOT", "query_str": "what is the capital of Australia and why is it not Sydney", "search_focus": "internet", "source": "default", "attachments": [], "updated_datetime": "2026-07-31T16:18:02.733774", "read_write_token": "REDACTED", "step_type": "FINAL", "author_id": "REDACTED", "author_username": "REDACTED", "author_image": "REDACTED", "bookmark_state": "NOT_BOOKMARKED", "s3_social_preview_url": "https://ppl-ai-public.s3.amazonaws.com/static/img/pplx-default-preview.png", "thread_access": 1, "thread_url_slug": "9bf48727-3062-4a4c-998b-d798b74c78c0", "prompt_source": "user", "query_source": "home", "plan": {"goals": [{"id": "0", "description": "Searching the web", "final": true, "todo_task_status": "INCOMPLETE"}], "final": true}, "privacy_state": "NONE", "gpt4": false, "sources": {"sources": ["web"]}, "text_completed": true, "entry_created_datetime": "2026-07-31T16:17:55.115362+00:00", "entry_updated_datetime": "2026-07-31T16:18:02.665843+00:00", "blocks": [{"intended_usage": "plan", "plan_block": {"progress": "DONE", "goals": [{"id": "0", "description": "Searching the web", "final": true, "todo_task_status": "INCOMPLETE"}], "final": true}}, {"intended_usage": "ask_text_0_markdown", "markdown_block": {"progress": "DONE", "chunks": ["The capital of Australia is **Canberra**, not Sydney.[2][3][12]"], "chunk_starting_offset": 0, "answer": "The capital of Australia is **Canberra**, not Sydney.[2][3][12]", "inline_token_annotations": []}}, {"intended_usage": "ask_text_1_markdown", "markdown_block": {"progress": "DONE", "chunks": ["## Why Canberra, not Sydney?"], "chunk_starting_offset": 0, "answer": "## Why Canberra, not Sydney?", "inline_token_annotations": []}}, {"intended_usage": "ask_text_2_markdown", "markdown_block": {"progress": "DONE", "chunks": ["Canberra was chosen as Australia\u2019s capital in **1908** as a political compromise between the country\u2019s two largest and most rivalrous cities: **Sydney** and **Melbourne**.[4][6][10][11]\n\nWhen Australia federated in 1901, both Sydney (in New South Wales) and Melbourne (in Victoria) wanted to be the national capital. The dispute was so intense it threatened the unity of the new nation.[13][14]\n\nThe solution, written into **Section 125 of the Australian Constitution**, was:\n\n- The capital would be located **within New South Wales** (giving Sydney\u2019s state the honor)  \n- But it had to be **at least 100 miles (161 km) from Sydney** (so Sydney wouldn\u2019t dominate)  \n- Until the new capital was ready, **Melbourne would serve as the temporary seat of government**[7][15]\n\nCanberra, a rural area between the two cities, was selected in 1908, formally founded in **1913**, and the federal government finally moved there from Melbourne in **1927**.[10][4][7][13]"], "chunk_starting_offset": 0, "answer": "Canberra was chosen as Australia\u2019s capital in **1908** as a political compromise between the country\u2019s two largest and most rivalrous cities: **Sydney** and **Melbourne**.[4][6][10][11]\n\nWhen Australia federated in 1901, both Sydney (in New South Wales) and Melbourne (in Victoria) wanted to be the national capital. The dispute was so intense it threatened the unity of the new nation.[13][14]\n\nThe solution, written into **Section 125 of the Australian Constitution**, was:\n\n- The capital would be located **within New South Wales** (giving Sydney\u2019s state the honor)  \n- But it had to be **at least 100 miles (161 km) from Sydney** (so Sydney wouldn\u2019t dominate)  \n- Until the new capital was ready, **Melbourne would serve as the temporary seat of government**[7][15]\n\nCanberra, a rural area between the two cities, was selected in 1908, formally founded in **1913**, and the federal government finally moved there from Melbourne in **1927**.[10][4][7][13]", "inline_token_annotations": []}}, {"intended_usage": "ask_text_3_markdown", "markdown_block": {"progress": "DONE", "chunks": ["## What makes Canberra unique?"], "chunk_starting_offset": 0, "answer": "## What makes Canberra unique?", "inline_token_annotations": []}}, {"intended_usage": "ask_text_4_markdown", "markdown_block": {"progress": "DONE", "chunks": ["- It\u2019s a **purpose-built, planned city**, designed by American architect Walter Burley Griffin.[6][13]\n- It\u2019s Australia\u2019s **largest inland city**, located in the **Australian Capital Territory (ACT)**, about 150\u2013240 km southwest of Sydney.[3][10][12]\n- Unlike most national capitals, it was never a major commercial or port city; it exists primarily as the **seat of government**.[13][14]"], "chunk_starting_offset": 0, "answer": "- It\u2019s a **purpose-built, planned city**, designed by American architect Walter Burley Griffin.[6][13]\n- It\u2019s Australia\u2019s **largest inland city**, located in the **Australian Capital Territory (ACT)**, about 150\u2013240 km southwest of Sydney.[3][10][12]\n- Unlike most national capitals, it was never a major commercial or port city; it exists primarily as the **seat of government**.[13][14]", "media_items": [{"medium": "image", "image": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/Overlooking_Canberra,_Parliament_House,_War_Memorial.jpg", "image_width": 2517, "image_height": 1564, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Australian_capital_cities", "name": "List of Australian capital cities - Wikipedia", "source": "sapi_images", "thumbnail": "https://d2u1z1lopyfwlx.cloudfront.net/thumbnails/27ddc6ff-34e4-5796-a9e8-305900caaab9/01a84265-e09c-5682-92ce-681c89a1afe2.jpg", "thumbnail_height": 318, "thumbnail_width": 512, "caption": "View of Canberra showing the Australian War Memorial, Anzac Parade leading across Lake Burley Griffin towards Parliament House on Capital Hill.", "citation_info": {"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Australian_capital_cities", "domain_name": "wikipedia", "favicon_url": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?sz=32&domain=en.wikipedia.org"}}], "inline_token_annotations": []}}, {"intended_usage": "ask_text_4_images", "inline_entity_block": {"media_block": {"media_items": [{"medium": "image", "image": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/Overlooking_Canberra,_Parliament_House,_War_Memorial.jpg", "image_width": 2517, "image_height": 1564, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Australian_capital_cities", "name": "List of Australian capital cities - Wikipedia", "source": "sapi_images", "thumbnail": "https://d2u1z1lopyfwlx.cloudfront.net/thumbnails/27ddc6ff-34e4-5796-a9e8-305900caaab9/01a84265-e09c-5682-92ce-681c89a1afe2.jpg", "thumbnail_height": 318, "thumbnail_width": 512, "caption": "View of Canberra showing the Australian War Memorial, Anzac Parade leading across Lake Burley Griffin towards Parliament House on Capital Hill.", "citation_info": {"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Australian_capital_cities", "domain_name": "wikipedia", "favicon_url": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?sz=32&domain=en.wikipedia.org"}}], "generated_media_items": []}}}, {"intended_usage": "ask_text_5_markdown", "markdown_block": {"progress": "DONE", "chunks": ["So Sydney remains Australia\u2019s largest and most internationally recognized city, but Canberra holds the official status of national capital as a deliberate compromise to balance regional rivalries.[2][11][15]"], "chunk_starting_offset": 0, "answer": "So Sydney remains Australia\u2019s largest and most internationally recognized city, but Canberra holds the official status of national capital as a deliberate compromise to balance regional rivalries.[2][11][15]", "inline_token_annotations": []}}, {"intended_usage": "ask_text", "markdown_block": {"progress": "DONE", "chunks": ["The capital of Australia i", "s **Canberra**,", " not Syd", "ney.[2][3]", "[12]", "\n", "## Why Canbe", "rra, not Syd", "ney?", "\n", "Canberra", " was chosen as Austr", "alia\u2019s capital i", "n **1908** as a polit", "ical compromise between", " the cou", "ntry\u2019s two largest", " and most rival", "rous cities: **Sydney** and **Melbourn", "e**.[4][6][10][11]\n\nWhen Australia f", "ederate", "d in 1901, ", "both Sydn", "ey (in New South Wa", "les) and Melbourne (in Vict", "oria) wa", "nted to be the nati", "onal capital. The dis", "pute was so intens", "e it threatened", " the unity of the new na", "t", "ion.[13][14]\n", "\nThe solut", "ion, written ", "into **Sectio", "n 125 of the Austra", "lian Constitution**, was:\n\n- The capital would be locate", "d **within New South Wal", "es** (giving Sydn", "ey\u2019s state", " the ho", "nor)  \n- But it", " had to be **at l", "east 100 m", "iles (16", "1 km) from Sydn", "ey** (so Sydney wo", "uldn\u2019t domin", "ate)  \n- Until the", " new capital was r", "eady, **Melbourne w", "ould serve as the temporary ", "seat of govern", "me", "nt**[7][15]\n", "\nCanbe", "rra, a r", "ural area bet", "ween", " the two cities, was sele", "cted in", " 1908, form", "ally founded i", "n **191", "3**, and the fed", "eral government fin", "ally moved there ", "from Melbourne in ", "**192", "7**.[10][4][7][13]", "\n", "## What makes Canberra uni", "que?", "\n", "- It\u2019s a **pur", "pose-built, planned ", "city**, designed by Amer", "ican architect Wa", "lter Burley Grif", "fin.[6][13]\n- ", "It\u2019s Austr", "alia\u2019s **largest in", "land city**, located in", " the **Australian Capital Territo", "ry (ACT", ")**, about", " 150\u2013240 km south", "west of Syd", "ney.[3][10]", "[12]\n- Unlike ", "most nati", "onal capitals", ", it was n", "ever a major commer", "cial or ", "port ", "city; it ex", "ists primarily as", " the **", "seat of govern", "men", "t**.", "[13][14]", "\n", "So Sydney rem", "ains Australia\u2019s largest", " and most internation", "ally recogn", "ized city, but Canb", "erra holds the official st", "atus of nati", "onal capita", "l as a deliberate compro", "mise to bal", "ance regional r", "ivalr", "ies.[2][11][15]"], "chunk_starting_offset": 0, "answer": "The capital of Australia is **Canberra**, not Sydney.[2][3][12]\n## Why Canberra, not Sydney?\nCanberra was chosen as Australia\u2019s capital in **1908** as a political compromise between the country\u2019s two largest and most rivalrous cities: **Sydney** and **Melbourne**.[4][6][10][11]\n\nWhen Australia federated in 1901, both Sydney (in New South Wales) and Melbourne (in Victoria) wanted to be the national capital. The dispute was so intense it threatened the unity of the new nation.[13][14]\n\nThe solution, written into **Section 125 of the Australian Constitution**, was:\n\n- The capital would be located **within New South Wales** (giving Sydney\u2019s state the honor)  \n- But it had to be **at least 100 miles (161 km) from Sydney** (so Sydney wouldn\u2019t dominate)  \n- Until the new capital was ready, **Melbourne would serve as the temporary seat of government**[7][15]\n\nCanberra, a rural area between the two cities, was selected in 1908, formally founded in **1913**, and the federal government finally moved there from Melbourne in **1927**.[10][4][7][13]\n## What makes Canberra unique?\n- It\u2019s a **purpose-built, planned city**, designed by American architect Walter Burley Griffin.[6][13]\n- It\u2019s Australia\u2019s **largest inland city**, located in the **Australian Capital Territory (ACT)**, about 150\u2013240 km southwest of Sydney.[3][12][10]\n- Unlike most national capitals, it was never a major commercial or port city; it exists primarily as the **seat of government**.[14][13]\nSo Sydney remains Australia\u2019s largest and most internationally recognized city, but Canberra holds the official status of national capital as a deliberate compromise to balance regional rivalries.[11][15][2]"}}, {"intended_usage": "workflow_root", "workflow_block": {"version": "1.0", "status": "WORKFLOW_COMPLETED", "headline": "", "completed_at": "", "predicted_completion_at": "", "steps": [{"status": "WORKFLOW_COMPLETED", "title": "Searching the web", "items": [{"id": "8641b306-7fe7-4cae-bebd-9ff4634c51aa", "type": "WORKFLOW_ITEM_QUERIES", "payload": {"queries_payload": {"queries": ["capital of Australia", "why is Canberra capital not Sydney"]}}}, {"id": "c52f6f8b-71d7-4fd8-83f3-b0453f36addd", "type": "WORKFLOW_ITEM_SOURCES", "payload": {"sources_payload": {"sources": [{"name": "Canberra - Wikipedia", "snippet": "", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra", "meta_data": {"client": "web", "date": "2001-08-27", "domain_name": "Wikimedia Foundation, Inc.", "published_date": "2001-08-27T00:00:00"}, "is_attachment": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false, "trust": {"level": 2, "name": "trusted", "description": "is trusted for broad, cited secondary-reference information across education, science, history, and general knowledge"}}, {"name": "Australia | History, Cities, Population, Capital, Map, & Facts", "snippet": "Australia is the smallest continent and one of the largest countries on Earth, lying between the Pacific and Indian oceans in the Southern Hemisphere. Its capital city is Canberra, and its most important economic and cultural centers are Sydney and Melbourne.", "url": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Australia", "meta_data": {"client": "web", "date": "2026-06-08", "domain_name": "Encyclopedia Britannica", "description": "Australia is the smallest continent and one of the largest countries on Earth, lying between the Pacific and Indian oceans in the Southern Hemisphere. Its capital city is Canberra, and its most important economic and cultural centers are Sydney and Melbourne.", "published_date": "2026-06-08T00:00:00"}, "is_attachment": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false, "trust": {"level": 2, "name": "trusted", "description": "is trusted for professionally edited general-reference and educational articles across history, science, culture, and other subjects"}}, {"name": "What is the Capital of Australia? - Mappr", "snippet": "The capital of Australia is Canberra. The city is located in the Australian Capital Territory, 150 kilometers inland from the country\u2019s southeast coast.", "url": "https://www.mappr.co/capital-cities/australia/", "meta_data": {"client": "web", "date": "2024-03-04", "domain_name": "Mappr", "description": "The capital of Australia is Canberra. The city is located in the Australian Capital Territory, 150 kilometers inland from the country\u2019s southeast coast.", "published_date": "2024-03-04T00:00:00"}, "is_attachment": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false}, {"name": "What is the Capital of Australia? Canberra Facts & History - USAnalysis.org", "snippet": "You\u2019ve probably been asked \u201cWhat is the capital of Australia?\u201d more than once. The answer is Canberra \u2014 but the story behind that answer is a fascinating tale of political compromise, rivalries, and a purpose-built city. Official capital: Canberra \u00b7 Population of Canberra (2021): 484,630 \u00b7 Year named capital: 1913 \u00b7 Federal territory: Australian Capital [\u2026]", "url": "https://usanalysis.org/blog/what-is-the-capital-of-australia/", "meta_data": {"client": "web", "date": "2026-07-16", "domain_name": "usanalysis.org", "description": "You\u2019ve probably been asked \u201cWhat is the capital of Australia?\u201d more than once. The answer is Canberra \u2014 but the story behind that answer is a fascinating tale of political compromise, rivalries, and a purpose-built city. Official capital: Canberra \u00b7 Population of Canberra (2021): 484,630 \u00b7 Year named capital: 1913 \u00b7 Federal territory: Australian Capital [\u2026]", "published_date": "2026-07-16T00:00:00"}, "is_attachment": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false}, {"name": "Australia - Wikipedia", "snippet": "", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia", "meta_data": {"client": "web", "date": "2001-11-04", "domain_name": "Wikimedia Foundation, Inc.", "published_date": "2001-11-04T00:00:00"}, "is_attachment": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false, "trust": {"level": 2, "name": "trusted", "description": "is trusted for broad, cited secondary-reference information across education, science, history, and general knowledge"}}, {"name": "Portal:Geography/Featured article/28 - Wikipedia", "snippet": "", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portal:Geography/Featured_article/28", "m