rusted for broad, cited secondary-reference information across education, science, history, and general knowledge"}}, "status": "UNSORTED", "citation": 6}, {"web_result": {"name": "List of Australian capital cities - Wikipedia", "snippet": "There are eight capital cities in Australia, each of which functions as the seat of government for the state or territory in which it is located. One of these, Canberra, is also the national capital. Section 125 of the Constitution of Australia specified that the seat of the national government, that is, the national capital, would be in its own territory within New South Wales, at least 100 miles (161 km) from Sydney. The Constitution specified that until this national capital was ready, the...", "timestamp": "2005-12-05T00:00:00", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Australian_capital_cities", "meta_data": {"citation_domain_name": null, "client": "web", "images": ["https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Skylines_of_Sydney_CBD_seen_from_North_Sydney%2C_August_2022%2C_04.jpg/1280px-Skylines_of_Sydney_CBD_seen_from_North_Sydney%2C_August_2022%2C_04.jpg"]}, "is_attachment": false, "is_image": false, "is_code_interpreter": false, "is_knowledge_card": false, "is_navigational": false, "is_widget": false, "is_focused_web": false, "is_client_context": false, "is_memory": false, "is_conversation_history": false, "is_conversation_summary": false, "trust": {"level": 2, "name": "trusted", "description": "is trusted for broad, cited secondary-reference information across education, science, history, and general knowledge"}}, "status": "UNSORTED", "citation": 7}, {"web_result": {"name": "How Canberra Became the Capital of Australia", "snippet": "Wondering why Canberra, not Sydney or Melbourne, is the capital of Australia? Discover how it was chosen, what makes it unique, and why it\u2019s worth visiting.", "timestamp": "2025-05-29T00:00:00", "url": "https://www.remitly.com/blog/en-au/lifestyle-culture/capital-of-a